[
  {
    "id": "p-7a294a",
    "offset": 0,
    "text": "27. The Lovers' Talk\nGirl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-91c5ef",
    "offset": 27,
    "text": "Wise Helen was carried off by Paris, another cowherd."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 82,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-5d9113",
    "offset": 91,
    "text": "Rather it was Helen who, of her own will, kissed the cowherd and kept him."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 167,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-f1e451",
    "offset": 173,
    "text": "Do not boast, little satyr; an empty thing, they say, is a kiss."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 239,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-280d24",
    "offset": 248,
    "text": "Even in empty kisses there is a sweet delight."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 296,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d5a4be",
    "offset": 302,
    "text": "I wash my mouth and spit away your kiss."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 344,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-67230c",
    "offset": 353,
    "text": "You wash your lips? Give them again, that I may kiss you."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 412,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-5ddd36",
    "offset": 418,
    "text": "It becomes you to kiss your heifers, not an unwedded girl."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 478,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-b5816b",
    "offset": 487,
    "text": "Do not boast; for soon your youth passes by like a dream."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 546,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-f0e57b",
    "offset": 552,
    "text": "And if I grow somewhat old, I drink, no doubt, honey and milk for that."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 625,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c18688",
    "offset": 634,
    "text": ". . ."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 641,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-7dea9c",
    "offset": 647,
    "text": "The grape becomes a raisin, and the dried rose will not perish."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 712,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-33f09b",
    "offset": 721,
    "text": "Come here, under the wild olives, that I may tell you a tale."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 784,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-491f5c",
    "offset": 790,
    "text": "I will not; before now you beguiled me with a sweet tale."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 849,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-445bb8",
    "offset": 858,
    "text": "Come here, under the elms, that you may hear my pipe."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 913,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-166516",
    "offset": 919,
    "text": "Delight your own heart; nothing sad can please me."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 971,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-6d495c",
    "offset": 980,
    "text": "Alas, alas, you too, girl, beware the wrath of the Paphian."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1041,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-614e02",
    "offset": 1047,
    "text": "Farewell to the Paphian; only let Artemis be gracious to me."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1109,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-2f5f4f",
    "offset": 1118,
    "text": "Do not say it, lest she strike you and you fall into an inextricable net."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1193,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-572775",
    "offset": 1199,
    "text": "Let her strike as she will; Artemis again will help me."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1256,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-362030",
    "offset": 1265,
    "text": "You do not escape Love, whom no other maiden escaped."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1320,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-59130c",
    "offset": 1326,
    "text": "I escape him, by Pan; but you ever bear his yoke."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1377,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d1e7f7",
    "offset": 1386,
    "text": "I fear lest she give you to a worse man."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1428,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-681232",
    "offset": 1434,
    "text": "Many have wooed me, but none has won my heart."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1482,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-e8b506",
    "offset": 1491,
    "text": "I too come here, one of many, your suitor."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1535,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-7c7f6a",
    "offset": 1541,
    "text": "And what shall I do, friend? Marriages are full of troubles."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1603,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-5966c9",
    "offset": 1612,
    "text": "Marriage holds no pain, no grief, but dancing."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1660,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-86cf81",
    "offset": 1666,
    "text": "Yes, but they say women dread their husbands."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1713,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-ddedb4",
    "offset": 1722,
    "text": "Rather they always rule them; whom do women dread?"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1774,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-45272b",
    "offset": 1780,
    "text": "I dread childbirth; harsh is the dart of Eileithyia."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1834,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d5d739",
    "offset": 1843,
    "text": "But Artemis, your queen, eases the pangs of birth."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 1895,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-532a58",
    "offset": 1901,
    "text": "But I dread to bear a child, lest I lose my fair beauty too."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 1963,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-32fde3",
    "offset": 1972,
    "text": "But if you bear dear children, you will see your sons as a new light."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 2043,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-0441f7",
    "offset": 2049,
    "text": "And what wedding-gift do you bring me, worthy of marriage, if I consent?"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 2123,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-7d22db",
    "offset": 2132,
    "text": "All my herd you shall have, all the groves and the pasture."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 2193,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-e52745",
    "offset": 2199,
    "text": "Swear that you will not, when the wedding is done, leave me against my will and go."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 2284,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-34f50f",
    "offset": 2293,
    "text": "By Pan himself, no, not even if you should wish to drive me off."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 2359,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d57a16",
    "offset": 2365,
    "text": "Will you build me bridal chambers, will you build a house and courtyards?"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 2440,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-8dba56",
    "offset": 2449,
    "text": "I will build you bridal chambers; and the fair flocks I tend."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 2512,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-bb3a45",
    "offset": 2518,
    "text": "But to my aged father, what tale shall I tell, what story?"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 2578,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-1a5b85",
    "offset": 2587,
    "text": "He will approve your marriage, when he hears my name."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 2642,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-7aab32",
    "offset": 2648,
    "text": "Tell me that name of yours; even a name often gives delight."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 2710,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c632ad",
    "offset": 2719,
    "text": "I am Daphnis, and Lycidas is my father, and my mother Nomaea."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-228181",
    "offset": 2782,
    "text": "Girl"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-38088f",
    "offset": 2788,
    "text": "You are of good birth; but I am no meaner than you."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-07e2c8",
    "offset": 2841,
    "text": "Daphnis"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-79f939",
    "offset": 2850,
    "text": "I know, you are of the highest honor; and your father is Menalcas."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c18688",
    "offset": 2918,
    "text": ". . ."
  }
]